  "body": "# HyperFrames v0.9.7\n\nReleased on 2026-11-03.\n\nStudio playback no longer freezes WebGL scenes when motion blur is on. Preview playback now lands on the same frame as a scrub or an export when a set cuts into a running tween. Your CLI login now takes priority over an API key left in your shell.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Lint:** `overlapping_gsap_tweens` now also flags a `set` that fires while a tween on the same element and property is still running, a pattern that plays differently from how it scrubs and exports ([5e30bbdbe](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/5e30bbdbe14b8295f8102c6439aa8bfdacc0fd1e), [#7059](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7059)).\n- **Preview:** A video the browser cannot play, such as HEVC without a decoder or ProRes, shows its own frame at the playhead instead of black while its playable copy is made. Copy progress is now reported at Full quality too ([eb3562966](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/eb3562966fcbac74da75566b660cbb41aa940739), [#6589](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/6589)).\n\n## Fixes\n\n- **Studio:** With motion blur on, a scene that draws to a WebGL canvas no longer freezes during preview playback. Motion blur now falls back for those scenes, as it already did in renders ([112ba5330](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/112ba53302726f2135dc7b28b03033b5a897ffbd), [#7060](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7060)).\n- **Core:** Preview playback now lands on the same frame as a scrub or an export when a `set` fires inside a running tween on the same property. Before, a word hidden just before its pop-in ended could stay on screen while playing ([0f85af7c7](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/0f85af7c7fd90ab755cd6f5c7f879eef7ed2aacc), [#7061](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7061)).\n- **CLI:** `hyperframes cloud render` no longer offers `--page-motion-blur`, because the hosted render API rejected requests that used it. Turn motion blur on in the composition with `data-motion-blur=\"on\"`. Local `hyperframes render --page-motion-blur` is unchanged ([dffc640e8](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/dffc640e8556b675e7e1d73f482c19ee7e855782), [#7062](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7062)).\n- **CLI:** A session from `hyperframes auth login` now takes priority over `HEYGEN_API_KEY` and `HYPERFRAMES_API_KEY`, so a key left in your shell no longer replaces the account you signed in with. The key still wins when `HEYGEN_API_URL` or `HEYGEN_API_BASE` points at another host, or when the login cannot refresh ([d03bdeae9](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/d03bdeae9d992c9bb653bb1e67cf5569d16455f3), [#7051](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7051)).\n- **Studio Server:** Two exports of the same project started within one second now get their own jobs and output files. Before, the second export replaced the first ([92943d99f](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/92943d99f08394b4a9d3964471ccae1bb86c83de), [#7053](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7053)).\n- **CLI:** `hyperframes snapshot` no longer crashes Chrome on a project with many clips cut from one 4K video. Like render, it now stops Chrome from decoding local videos it already replaces with extracted frames ([81b93cf05](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/81b93cf055dee34ec1e47e1e64e0c5bba35aef05), [#6949](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/6949)).\n- **CLI:** The `latestVersion` value in `--json` output is never older than the CLI you are running, even right after an upgrade ([8a6636efe](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/8a6636efe36c3ec313aeb4a122f875b687ffdc5d), [#7049](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7049)).\n- **CLI:** `hyperframes auth login --device` now works without a terminal, such as in a coding agent's shell or an SSH command. It still refuses to run in CI ([de2603e63](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/de2603e637f09fc0490d06bf92151dddc8d0650f), [#7045](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7045)).\n\n## Docs & Examples\n\n- **Skills:** The reverse skill asks once for a credit top-up that covers the whole run when several steps run out at the same time, and builds its project with `init --video` ([05ddddbbf](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/05ddddbbf08fd358b5879726f935d5414733da3a), [#7048](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7048)).\n- **Changelog:** Added the weekly update for October 26 to November 2, 2026 ([6feb4bec7](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/6feb4bec7aa046a8956efd8a718db55423e2e2ca), [#7032](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7032)).\n- **Changelog:** The v0.9.6 release notes now list four changes they had missed ([4ef8c1de5](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/4ef8c1de5cfc298bdbd385decd3a95b0ef301adc), [#7040](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7040)).\n\n## Internal\n\n- **Studio Server:** Raised the package size budget to fit the new preview features ([b22af8f25](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/commit/b22af8f25ccc155b38b3501ddada92ff9e855503), [#7044](https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/pull/7044)).\n\n## Full changelog\n\nhttps://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/compare/v0.9.6...v0.9.7\n"
}
